In article <4539@ucsbcsl.ucsb.edu> hench@gauss.UUCP (John Hench) writes:
|I have a question. If you had a 10 wishes, what things would you wish for and
|why. Also, how would you rank the item's usefulness? My list:



|Excaliber

Don't bother.  Get a long sword and #dip it.  Don't waste a wish.

|gray dragon scale mail

Okay, but wouldn't you rather make your own?  

|helm of telepathy

Very useful, very rare.

|gauntlets of power

Dexterity, not strength.  Strength you get from spinach, dead giants, and
royal jelly.  Str 25 is worse than 18/** in terms of carrying capacity.
Dex affects how likely you are to hit, so adding two or three points adds lots
of hits.

|speed boots

Elven boots are better, except when you need to cross trapdoors and pools.
Elven boots are not rare.  Don't waste a wish on boots.

|wand of death

very useful, very rare.

|cloak of displacement

|blessed scroll of genocide (I hate liches!)

so do I.  But excalibur, good str, good AC, and they're dead meat.
(don't forget to teleport outta there when hp<50.)

|shield of relection

|luckstone

blessed luckstone, please.

If your luck is good, an amulet of life saving is useful.
If you have a bunch of useless scrolls and water to dip them in, a blessed
magic marker(100) can come in very handy.
So can a spellbook of remove curse. or of identify.
remember to keep your unicorn horn blessed or uncursed.  Got killed recently
by a cursed horn.
If you are desprate for an intinsic, 3 blessed tins of <monster with that 
intrinsic>.

Keep hacking!

